---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy · b-ark · b-oss"
  description="Privacy policy for b-ark — the Windows desktop app that backs up your Blipfoto journal to a folder on your own computer."
  narrow
>
  <Hero label="Privacy hero" title="Privacy Policy — b-ark">b-ark is a Windows desktop app that backs up your Blipfoto journal to a folder on your own
      computer. This policy explains what data the app handles and where it goes.</Hero>

  <section
    class="block"
    style="border-top: none; padding-top: 0"
    data-screen-label="Privacy body"
  >
    <p><em>Last updated: 3 November 2026</em></p>

    <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
    <p>
      b-ark is an open-source project, part of b-oss and led by Ian Stevenson. It is an
      independent app built on Blipfoto's public API, and is not affiliated with or endorsed by
      Blipfoto. Questions about this policy can be sent to
      <a href="mailto:info@b-oss.dev">info@b-oss.dev</a> or through the
      <a href="contact">contact page</a>, whose form is delivered by
      <a href="https://web3forms.com/privacy">Web3Forms</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>What stays on your computer</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Your backups, in the folder you choose.</li>
      <li>The app's settings.</li>
      <li>
        Your Blipfoto sign-in details, which are encrypted using the operating system's secure
        storage.
      </li>
      <li>A log file, written on your computer only.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>None of this is sent to the b-oss project.</p>

    <h2>What is sent to Blipfoto</h2>
    <p>
      The app connects to Blipfoto (its API, your pictures, and the Blipfoto website where a
      backup needs it) to back up your journal. That traffic is between your computer and
      Blipfoto, under Blipfoto's own privacy policy. The b-oss project does not receive a copy.
    </p>

    <h2>Updates</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>If you downloaded b-ark from this website,</strong> the app by default checks for
      updates by contacting GitHub, where the b-oss releases are published, and downloads a new
      version if there is one. GitHub can see that request under
      <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">its privacy statement</a>.
      You can turn this off in the app's settings.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>If you installed b-ark through the Microsoft Store,</strong> Microsoft handles
      updates, under Microsoft's own privacy policy.
    </p>

    <h2>What the app does not do</h2>
    <p>
      It has no analytics and no crash reporting, and sends nothing to the b-oss project. The
      app has no server of its own.
    </p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      Everything the app holds is on your computer and under your control. Data held by
      Blipfoto is managed through Blipfoto.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      If this policy changes materially, the updated version will be published at this URL with
      a revised date at the top.
    </p>
  </section>
</Layout>
